From e284d53c6f2edd9ed949752b32e6720136336b1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:30:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Push notices, ready to turn on with the Firebase
 project

After the login the app asks for the permission and registers the phone
at care/push-devices; a renewed token is registered again. A tapped
notice opens the conversation or the agenda (the paths of the web app),
one that arrives with the app open shows at the bottom. At the logout
the phone is removed while the login still works, so the next person
on the phone does not get the notices. Off unless the build has the
Firebase values (--dart-define FCM_API_KEY, FCM_APP_ID, FCM_SENDER_ID,
FCM_PROJECT_ID); a failure never blocks the app.

Notices that arrive with the app closed use the ALMOVA "A" as icon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
